sh)\">\\(\\mathrm{Logic}(F,\\vdash)\\)</span>; finitarity is one clause of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"bd7e4207897c8db3\" href=\"?note=bd7e4207897c8db3\" title=\"93-df-logic\">93-df-logic</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\\subseteq F\">\\(\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}\\)</span> is the maximal-consistent-theory predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"8bbd77b21a9519f1\" href=\"?note=8bbd77b21a9519f1\" title=\"93-df-maximal-theory\">93-df-maximal-theory</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}lindembaum}\\vdash\n\\mathsf L=\\langle F,\\vdash\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}(F,\\vdash)\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\n\\to\\exists\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\bigl(\\Gamma\\subseteq\\Delta\\land\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(\\Delta,\\mathsf L)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}lindembaum}\\vdash\n\\mathsf L=\\langle F,\\vdash\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Logic}(F,\\vdash)\n\\land\\mathrm{Cons}_{93}(\\Gamma,\\mathsf L)\n\\to\\exists\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\bigl(\\Gamma\\subseteq\\Delta\\land\\mathrm{MaxTh}_{93}(\\Delta,\\mathsf L)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Finitarity ensures that the union of a chain of consistent theories is\nconsistent, so Zorn's lemma supplies a maximal consistent extension.  The displayed pair equality ensures that consistency, maximality, and the quantified carrier all refer to the same logic.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[